# Decision log

Choices that shaped the analysis, in the order they were made, including where the work departs from the original brief. Numbers are rendered from `reports/metrics.json`.

## Scope and target

1. **Window changed from 2015-2018 to 36-month loans issued 2012-2015.** At the data snapshot {{ m.censoring.share_36m_2016 | pct(0) }} of 36-month 2016 loans and {{ m.censoring.share_36m_2017 | pct(0) }} of 2017 loans were still running. Keeping only their resolved loans would select early defaults and early payoffs. In the chosen window only {{ m.censoring.scope_non_terminal_share | pct(2) }} of loans are unresolved (`reports/tables/censoring_by_vintage.csv`). The 2015 vintage was checked separately: {{ m.censoring.share_36m_2015 | pct(2) }} unresolved, so no adjustment to the window was needed.
2. **60-month loans excluded** ({{ m.censoring.share_60m_2015 | pct(0) }} of the 2015 vintage still running, different risk profile). Next step once more vintages resolve.
3. **Joint applications excluded** ({{ d.joint_excluded | num }} loans). They appear only from October 2015, so the model could not learn them.
4. **Target:** Charged Off or Default = 1, Fully Paid = 0. The {{ d.non_terminal_excluded | num }} loans still current, in grace or late are excluded and counted by vintage (`reports/tables/scope_flow.csv`).
5. **Split by issue month:** train 2012-01 to 2014-12, validation 2015-01 to 2015-06, test 2015-07 to 2015-12. No random split anywhere. No sampling: all {{ d.sample_rows | num }} loans are used.

## Features

6. **Every raw column has a written decision** (`docs/feature_audit.csv`, {{ au.n_columns }} rows). Kept: {{ au.by_decision.keep }} application fields plus {{ au.by_decision.transformed }} transformed into derived features.
7. **Lending Club's grade, sub-grade, interest rate and instalment are not features.** They are the incumbent model; the sub-grade is the benchmark and the rate drives the P&L.
8. **Proxy fields dropped:** `zip_code`, `addr_state` (geography) and `emp_title` (free text, very high cardinality).
9. **Late-2015 bureau fields dropped** ({{ au.by_category.late_2015_field }} columns): empty for the whole training window.
10. **Missing values kept as information.** `mths_since_last_delinq` is missing when the applicant has never been delinquent; LightGBM learns a direction for missing values and the scorecard gives them their own bin.

## Models

11. **Scorecard selection:** IV at least {{ md.selection.iv_min | dec }}, drop the weaker of any pair with WoE correlation above {{ md.selection.corr_max | dec(1) }}, add characteristics in IV order only if validation AUC rises by {{ md.selection.min_gain | dec(4) }} or more and every coefficient keeps the expected sign. Result: {{ md.scorecard.n_characteristics }} characteristics (`reports/tables/scorecard_selection.csv`).
12. **LightGBM:** 6-configuration grid on leaves and minimum leaf size, learning rate 0.05, early stopping on validation AUC, 4 threads, deterministic mode. Best: {{ md.lgbm.best_params.num_leaves }} leaves, {{ md.lgbm.best_params.min_data_in_leaf }} minimum rows per leaf, {{ md.lgbm.best_iteration }} trees.
13. **Recalibration on validation (Platt) for all three rankers.** Trained on a calmer period, the models under-predicted 2015 defaults.

## Business layer

14. **Cash definitions checked before use:** `total_pymnt` = principal + interest + late fees + recoveries on every loan (largest gap {{ p.cash.identity_max_abs_residual | dec }} dollars). Lender cash = `total_pymnt` minus `collection_recovery_fee`.
15. **G and L measured on training loans only**, amount-weighted; low/high = best and worst training year.
16. **Cost of funds and opex are stated assumptions** (base {{ p.assumptions.cost_of_funds.base | pct }} a year and {{ p.assumptions.opex.base | pct }} of principal), editable in the simulator.
17. **Cutoff chosen on validation** by expected profit with a {{ rec.min_volume | pct(0) }} approval floor; test used once.
18. **Plain PD cutoff preferred to a price-aware margin rule**, which earned {{ p.price_aware.gap_vs_pd_cutoff | susd }} relative to it on test.
19. **Headline impact uses realized cash**, because expected profit overstated realized profit by {{ p.expected_vs_realized_gap | pct }} of the test book.
20. **Annualisation:** twice the six-month test window, stated wherever an annual number appears.
